body:
Feature Request / Improvement
Problem. iceberg-aws declares the AWS SDK as compileOnly and the docs tell users to bring either the SDK bundle or "individual AWS client packages (Glue, S3, DynamoDB, KMS, STS)" (docs/docs/aws.md, "Enabling AWS Integration"). For S3FileIO alone, the set that is actually required at runtime is s3 plus kms and sts; glue and dynamodb are not needed. With only s3 (and an HTTP client) on the classpath, S3FileIO.initialize fails before any S3 call:
java.lang.NoClassDefFoundError: software/amazon/awssdk/services/kms/model/EncryptionAlgorithmSpec
    at org.apache.iceberg.aws.AwsProperties.<clinit>(AwsProperties.java:231)
    at org.apache.iceberg.aws.AwsClientFactories$DefaultAwsClientFactory.<init>(AwsClientFactories.java:101)
    at org.apache.iceberg.aws.AwsClientFactories.<clinit>(AwsClientFactories.java:50)

Add kms and it becomes:
java.lang.NoClassDefFoundError: software/amazon/awssdk/services/sts/model/Tag
    at org.apache.iceberg.aws.AwsProperties.toStsTags(AwsProperties.java:487)
    at org.apache.iceberg.aws.AwsProperties.<init>(AwsProperties.java:302)
    at org.apache.iceberg.aws.AwsClientFactories$DefaultAwsClientFactory.initialize(AwsClientFactories.java:179)

Add sts and initialization succeeds; glue and dynamodb make no difference. Verified on 1.12.0 with SDK 2.54.17 (JDK 21); AwsProperties, AwsClientFactories and the iceberg-aws build block are unchanged on main (2742348).
Cause. S3FileIO.initialize -> S3FileIOAwsClientFactories.initialize falls back to AwsClientFactories.from(...) when s3.client-factory-impl is unset -> AwsClientFactories.<clinit> builds DefaultAwsClientFactory, whose constructor and initialize eagerly build AwsProperties. AwsProperties has a static field of type kms.model.EncryptionAlgorithmSpec and its constructor calls toStsTags, so the KMS and STS model classes are loaded even though the S3-only path never uses them.
This is a smaller, precise instance of #7516 (avoid loading all AWS client dependencies): the S3-only factory from #7590 helps only when s3.client-factory-impl is set explicitly; the default path still pulls KMS and STS.
Reproduction. Classpath: org.apache.iceberg:iceberg-aws:1.12.0, iceberg-core:1.12.0, software.amazon.awssdk:s3:2.54.17, software.amazon.awssdk:url-connection-client:2.54.17; no kms, no sts.
import java.util.Map;
import org.apache.iceberg.aws.s3.S3FileIO;

public class InitS3FileIO {
  public static void main(String[] args) {
    try (S3FileIO io = new S3FileIO()) {
      io.initialize(Map.of());
      System.out.println("initialize OK");
    } catch (Throwable t) {
      System.out.println("initialize FAILED: " + t);
      t.printStackTrace(System.out);
    }
  }
}
Proposal.

Build AwsProperties lazily in DefaultAwsClientFactory: keep the property map, construct AwsProperties on first use in glue(), kms() and dynamo() (3 call sites plus a private accessor; about 15 changed lines in one class). With that change the program above prints initialize OK on the S3-only classpath, and a real exists() call builds the S3 client and fails only with ConnectException against a closed port. Prototype diff below (compiled against the released jars and shadowed on the classpath; not yet run through the project's own test suite / Spotless).
Correct docs/docs/aws.md: for S3FileIO the minimal set is s3 + an HTTP client today (plus kms/sts until (1) lands); Glue and DynamoDB are only needed for GlueCatalog / DynamoDbCatalog / the DynamoDB lock manager.

Anything that constructs AwsProperties directly (AwsKeyManagementClient, assume-role factories, SigV4 REST auth) legitimately still needs KMS/STS; (1) only stops the S3-only default path from loading them. I can open the PR for both parts; a regression test would load S3FileIO through a class loader that refuses software.amazon.awssdk.services.kms.* and sts.*.

Prototype patch against the 1.12.0 sources
