Please describe the bug 🐞
Problem
truncate[W] on strings truncates to W code points (UnicodeUtil.truncateString), but TruncateString.project and projectStrict decide how to project startsWith/notStartsWith by comparing the prefix's String.length() (UTF-16 chars) with W.
A prefix with supplementary characters such as emoji can have length() == W and still have fewer than W code points. The projection then treats it as a full partition value and turns it into an equality, while the partition values of matching rows are longer.
Reproduce
Schema schema = new Schema(Types.NestedField.optional(1, "s", Types.StringType.get()));
PartitionSpec spec = PartitionSpec.builderFor(schema).truncate("s", 2).build();

// "😀" is 1 code point but 2 chars. A row "😀abc" lands in partition s_trunc = "😀a".
Projections.inclusive(spec).project(Expressions.startsWith("s", "😀"));
// actual:   ref(name="s_trunc") == "😀"         -> partition "😀a" is pruned
// expected: ref(name="s_trunc") startsWith "😀"

Projections.strict(spec).project(Expressions.notStartsWith("s", "😀"));
// actual:   ref(name="s_trunc") != "😀"         -> partition "😀a" is treated as all-matching
// expected: ref(name="s_trunc") notStartsWith "😀"
Impact

Inclusive projection prunes partitions that contain matching rows, so scans with such a startsWith filter silently return fewer rows.
Strict projection reports partitions as fully matching when none of their rows match, which affects residuals and partition-level decisions such as metadata-only deletes.

It only happens for string truncate partitions when the prefix's UTF-16 length equals the width but its code point count is smaller. ASCII and BMP-only prefixes are unaffected.
Proposed fix
Compare the prefix's code point count with the width in both methods. I have a fix with tests and can open a PR.
Willingness to contribute

 I can contribute a fix for this bug independently
 I would be willing to contribute a fix for this bug with guidance from the Iceberg community
 I cannot contribute a fix for this bug at this time
